From cd8ad2f8fd70cdaf69e1bda96474f973847a4967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jdistler <josephcd921@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 09:40:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] demux: adaptive: force monotonic segment timeline
 (adaptive-ts-force-playlist)

Restream HLS panels often emit inconsistent per-segment PTS: the live-edge
segment carries broadcast wall-clock PTS while later segments reset toward 0,
so the demux timeline jumps backward at segment boundaries. On iOS this stalls
the clock (frames read as minutes/hours "too late") -> ~10s freeze every
segment -> watchdog reconnect. VLC's existing per-segment continuity
(SynchronizationReference) handles this on desktop but not for these panels on
iOS. This is the documented "PTS restart after HLS discontinuity" problem.

Add adaptive-ts-force-playlist: FakeESOut maintains ONE shared offset mapping
the demux timestamps onto a strictly monotonic output timeline, re-anchoring
whenever the input DTS jumps (backward, or forward past 1s). The same offset is
applied to every ES (dts/pts) and to PCR, so A/V and the clock stay in lockstep
across the discontinuity. Off by default; opt-in per stream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
